Your MATLAB code is correct and will solve the system of equations for "x", "a", "b", and "c". The `solve` function will return a symbolic expression for the solutions, which you can then evaluate numerically if needed. Here's an example of how to do this:

```matlab
syms a b c p q r x
eq1 = ap + bq + cr == 28;
eq2 = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);

% Evaluate the solutions numerically
a_val = simplify(subs(sol, {p, q, r}, {1, 2, 3}));
b_val = simplify(substitute(sol, {p, q, r}, {1, 2, 3}));
