Here's a simple JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_ID}/${process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_TOKEN}`;
  const payload = {
    channel,
    text
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => console.log('Message posted to Slack:', data))
  .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Make sure to replace `process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_ID` and `process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_TOKEN` with your actual Slack webhook ID and token.

