Certainly! Here's an example PHP code that uses GROUP BY and HAVING clauses to identify loyal customers based on their purchasing patterns:

```php
<?php
// Connect to your database
$servername = "localhost";
$username = "username";
$password = "password";
$dbname = "database_name";

$conn = new mysqli($servername, $username, $password, $dbname);

// Check connection
if ($conn->connect_error) {
    die("Connection failed: " . $conn->connect_error);
}

// Query to find loyal customers
$sql = "SELECT customer_id, COUNT(*) AS purchase_count
FROM transactions
WHERE product_id = 'specific_product_id'
GROUP BY customer_id
HAVING purchase_count >= 3";

$result = $conn->query($sql);

// Display results
if ($result->num_rows > 0) {
    // output data of each row
    while($row = $result->fetch_assoc()) {
        echo "Customer ID: " . $row["customer_id"]. " - Purchase Count: " . $row["purchase_count"]. "<br>";
    }
} else {
    echo "0 results";
}

$conn->close();
?>
```

Replace `'specific_product_id'` with the actual ID of the product you want to track. This code will group the transactions by customer ID and count the number of purchases for each customer. It will then filter the results to only show customers who have purchased the specified product at least three times in a week.

Note that this code assumes you have a table named `transactions` with columns `customer_id`, `product_id`, and `purchase_date`. You may need to adjust the table name and column names to match your own database schema.

