Here's a Go code that identifies if a given sentence contains a double negative:

```go
package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"strings"
)

func main() {
	sentence := "He isn't not worried about the coronavirus situation"
	negativeWords := []string{"not", "never", "no", "none", "nothing"}

	for _, word := range negativeWords {
		if strings.Contains(sentence, word) && strings.Contains(sentence, "not")+1 == strings.Index(sentence, word) {
			fmt.Println("The sentence contains a double negative.")
			break
		}
	}
}
```

This code defines a slice of specific negative words and checks if the sentence contains any of them, as well as the phrase "not" followed by that negative word. If both conditions are satisfied, it prints a message indicating that the sentence contains a double negative.

